      "id": "cosmic",
      "name": "Cosmic",
      "description": "The blanket starts at the dorsal midline and spreads down and out from it, one continuous region with no holes in it and no islands off it. It runs from the poll to the croup - the whole length of the neck as well as the barrel, hanging off the crest the way it hangs off the back - and stops above the elbow and stifle, never onto a limb, never onto a hoof. Its lower boundary is a long soft fade rather than a line: there is no edge on this marking anywhere. Inside are stars, thickest near the topline and thinning toward the edge, with a planet or a spiral galaxy on a heavily marked horse. Where the blanket meets the mane or the tail base the colour runs on into the hair, deepening toward the tips.",
